    ('8414ca9b-404d-49df-9aa9-6fe545ccac80'::uuid, 'card_description', '5th-4th millennium BC unchambered long barrow in Hampshire. A medieval iron spearhead and a seax blade found inside -- later peoples revisiting a Neolithic mound and depositing objects within it.', 'An iron spearhead was recovered from inside Preston Candover Long Barrow, a scramasax reportedly from its edge. Its shape is disputed: the Ordnance Survey map classed it as a round barrow.', 'teaser-card-s009:8414ca9b-404d-49df-9aa9-6fe545ccac80:card_description', 'teaser-card-s009 (teaser-card): teaser card, 188 characters, checked PASS, web-verified VERIFIED', '89a6f9e9c840d8a6e52726185cb5f2e2095c10d4be41b38092fe4b4da14d3650|f5f6d66391b0eacf6b26a5a15ff1c7cc03acaf9bf8db9b803284fe15ae35be67|f5f6d66391b0eacf6b26a5a15ff1c7cc03acaf9bf8db9b803284fe15ae35be67', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-write-016", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "An iron spearhead was recovered from inside Preston Candover Long Barrow, a scramasax reportedly from its edge. Its shape is disputed: the Ordnance Survey map classed it as a round barrow."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-check-016 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "an iron spearhead was recovered from inside the barrow [S3]; a scramasax was reportedly found at the edge of the barrow [S4]; the barrow''s classification (its shape) is disputed [S5, S6]; the Ordnance Survey map classed it as a round barrow [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-verify-047 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Preston Candover Long Barrow is a long barrow (an unchambered long barrow) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preston_Candover_Long_Barrow]; It is 