    ('99685d28-2f4f-409e-9f18-04a1215a04d1'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Oval univallate fort above Burrington Combe in the Mendip Hills. The combe below has produced cemetery finds of long human occupation, including at Aveline''s Hole nearby.', 'In the Mendip Hills, the oval Iron Age hill fort of Burrington Camp overlooks Burrington Combe, where discoveries of cemeteries reveal a very long human occupation of the area.', 'teaser-card-s009:99685d28-2f4f-409e-9f18-04a1215a04d1:card_description', 'teaser-card-s009 (teaser-card): teaser card, 176 characters, checked PASS, web-verified VERIFIED', '8359fffee1a847cd328201fd84c69d1c321153adddba4c473362580b19f02396|630595d5b737d9642447676fd59d22cc977804a547c3b5e710df47e04e9e4162|630595d5b737d9642447676fd59d22cc977804a547c3b5e710df47e04e9e4162', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-write-019", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "In the Mendip Hills, the oval Iron Age hill fort of Burrington Camp overlooks Burrington Combe, where discoveries of cemeteries reveal a very long human occupation of the area."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-check-019 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Burrington Camp is in the Mendip Hills [S2]; it is a hill fort [S1]; it is Iron Age [S1]; it is oval [S4]; it overlooks Burrington Combe [S3]; archaeological discoveries of cemeteries were made in Burrington Combe [S3]; the cemeteries demonstrate a very long human occupation of the area [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-verify-056 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Burrington Camp is a hill fort (the kind of place the text is about) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burrington_Camp]; The hill fort dates to the 